H='（聽力稿，原題播放兩次）\n'
P='（聽力稿）選出最適合的回應：\n'
PIC='\n請選出符合描述的圖片。'
PS=[]
D=[
(1,H+'The boy and the girl are hiking on a cloudy day.'+PIC,['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-2',115,725,1265,1045)]),
(2,H+'The woman is going to make a birthday cake, so she bought some milk, bananas and two boxes of eggs.'+PIC,['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-2',115,1110,1265,1430)]),
(3,H+'The man and the woman are moving the table. The woman is pushing it and the man is pulling it.'+PIC,['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-2',115,1495,1265,1815)]),
(4,P+'Excuse me, how often does Bus 234 run?',['Every 20 minutes.','Here it comes. Let’s run to the bus.','It runs from City Park to City Library.'],[]),
(5,P+'Can I help you paint the walls this afternoon?',['Hmm, it’s a bright color.','Wait! The paint is still wet.','No, thanks. I can do it myself.'],[]),
(6,P+'There are only a few students in the classroom. Where are the others?',['On the playground.','They come from the USA.','Class begins in ten minutes.'],[]),
(7,P+'Why did Tina shout at you just now?',['Please don’t shout at her.','Oh, then I shouted back to her.','Hmm, I was playing music too loud.'],[]),
(8,P+'Dad and Mom will come home in an hour. Let’s clean up the living room now.',['Good. It’s finally clean.','Sorry. I’m busy at the moment.','Right, they’re in the living room.'],[]),
(9,P+'Did you meet Jason at the train station at 3 p.m.?',['No, I didn’t. I forgot all about it.','Of course. I’ll be happy to do it.','Well, see you later at the station.'],[]),
(10,P+'How did Linda park her car between the two big cars?',['By car.','She’s fine.','It took her some time.'],[]),
(11,P+'My husband doesn’t feel any better after taking the medicine. I’m worried.',['Don’t worry. He’s feeling much better now.','Don’t be. I think you should take him to another doctor.','The doctor didn’t tell him to take medicine.'],[]),
(12,H+'M: How are the pants, ma’am?\nW: Well, I like the color, but look, they’re a little short for me. What do you think?\nM: Do you plan to wear these pants to work or for something else?\nW: Oh, I’m going to wear them to a good friend’s party next week.\nM: Well, then, you’ll need a longer pair of pants. I’ll get another pair in the same color for you. It will only take a moment.\nW: OK, I’ll wait.\nQ: Who is the man?',['A clerk.','A waiter.','A mailman.'],[]),
(13,H+'M: I have a gift for you, dear. Open it.\nW: Wow! White strawberries!\nM: Yeah, I bought them at a farmer’s market.\nW: Thank you. They must be very expensive.\nM: Well, white strawberries usually cost four or five times more than red ones.\nW: Wow! Is it because they’re a new kind of fruit?\nM: You make a good point. What’s more, white strawberries are more difficult to grow than red ones.\nW: I see.\nQ: What are the man and the woman talking about?',['A farmer’s market.','A special kind of fruit.','Why white strawberries are popular.'],[]),
(14,H+'M: It’s hot today. Let’s go swimming this afternoon.\nW: Sorry, but we can’t.\nM: Why not?\nW: You know, we’re having a dry year. No swimming pools near our home are open to the public from the end of April.\nM: When will they open again?\nW: We’ll have to wait until the rainy season.\nM: That’s too pathetic.\nW: I know. I’d love to swim in cool water, too.\nQ: When the man says, “That’s too pathetic,” what does he mean?',['That’s too bad.','It’s nothing big.','It’s still too early.'],[]),
(15,H+'M: This way, Helen. Tom lives on the third floor. Let’s climb the stairs.\nW: Oh, the stairs are so small. This apartment building must be very old.\nM: Yeah, it’s at least fifty years old. Be careful! There are some small boxes on the stairs.\nW: Hey, it’s not right to put the boxes here. Ouch! My right foot hurts!\nM: What happened? Let me see. Oh, no, it’s a nail.\nW: Argh! Poor me!\nQ: How are the stairs to Tom’s home?',['They are large.','They are dangerous.','They are convenient.'],[]),
(16,H+'B: What does your father do, Linda?\nG: He draws and writes comics.\nB: Cool! He must love his job very much.\nG: Yeah, he does. However, he has little time for himself or for us.\nB: You mean that he spends a lot of time working?\nG: That’s it. He has to look for comic ideas all the time. Also, he must work very hard to keep his works fresh and interesting.\nB: Oh, I see.\nQ: What does the girl think of her father’s job?',['It is pretty easy.','He doesn’t really enjoy it.','He puts all his heart into it.'],[]),
(17,H+'M: Are you free this Saturday afternoon, Lisa?\nW: Yes, I am. What’s up?\nM: Well, I’d like to invite you and David to my new house around 2 p.m.. I moved in last weekend.\nW: Good. We’ll be there.\nM: I live at 45, Second Street. When you get to Beach Road, drive along, and turn right at Second Street. Go for two blocks, and you’ll see my house on your left.\nW: Got it.\nQ: Where does the man live?（選項見圖）',['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-4',135,975,1275,1285)]),
(18,H+'W: Today’s the first Wednesday of April. It’s also National Walking Day.\nM: Really? What’s the holiday for?\nW: Taking time to enjoy walking, of course. At least 30 minutes a day.\nM: Come on, in this busy, modern world, who has so much time for walking?\nW: I do. When going to work, I usually get off the bus two stops earlier, so I can walk to my office. Believe me, it’s good for health in the long run.\nM: Well, I’ll start to walk more when I have time.\nW: When?\nM: Umm…\nQ: What can we learn from the dialogue?',['The woman invites the man to go for a walk.','The man does not enjoy walking as much as the woman does.','Both the man and the woman usually take a walk in the morning.'],[]),
(19,H+'M: Tony’s already three. It’s time to teach him to read more.\nW: Yeah, I just thought about it last night. What should we do first?\nM: Buy more picture books for him.\nW: Maybe later. He already has at least one hundred books, dear.\nM: Oh, I see. How about giving him a reading corner?\nW: Great idea. The corner next to the sofa will be OK.\nM: Agreed. Let’s take away the boxes and bags.\nW: OK. Let’s do it right now.\nM: Good. After we finish, I’ll mop the floor.\nQ: What are the man and the woman going to do first?',['Mop the floor.','Move things away.','Go shopping for picture books.'],[]),
(20,H+'W: This umbrella looks good. How much is it?\nM: $1,499.\nW: $1,499! Um, maybe I don’t really need an umbrella now. Thank you.\nM: Wait. It’s raining, and you’ll need an umbrella. Look at these two umbrellas. They’re on sale. The green one costs $399, and the yellow one, $599. Which do you like?\nW: Let me look at them carefully. Hmm, not bad. Both are good, but I like the color yellow better.\nM: Hmm, you have an eye for umbrellas.\nQ: How much is the woman going to spend on a new umbrella?',['$399.','$599.','$1,499.'],[]),
(21,H+'（廣播提示音）W: Good afternoon, everyone. This is Green Town Station. We need to let you know that Train 1891 from River Town to White Beach is running late. This is because of the strong wind and the heavy rain in Rainbow Town. The train has to stop at Spring Town Station for now. When the weather gets better, the train will leave for Rainbow Town Station, and then arrive at Green Town Station. Before then, please wait for around 20 minutes.\nQ: Which is the correct order of the stops for Train 1891?',['River Town→Rainbow Town→Spring Town→Green Town→White Beach.','River Town→Spring Town→Rainbow Town→Green Town→White Beach.','River Town→Spring Town→Green Town→Rainbow Town→White Beach.'],[]),
]
